  "notes": "Deeply rooted in Japanese folklore where foxes ({狐|きつね}) and tanuki ({狸|たぬき}) are believed to have shapeshifting powers. The figurative sense 2 is common in sports and business contexts.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {狐|きつね}が{化|ば}ける — a fox transforms\n- {大化|おおば}けする — to undergo a huge transformation\n- {化|ば}けの{皮|かわ}が{剥|は}がれる — one's true colors are revealed (lit. the disguise peels off)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {変身|へんしん}する — to transform (more neutral, used for heroes/costumes)\n- {変|か}わる — to change (general)",
